    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Fiendish Contract",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "downtime",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "The fiend caller spends 1 day of downtime setting up a bargain between a mortal creature and a fiend the fiend caller knows well. The fiend caller attempts a Legal Lore check against the higher of the fiend's Will DC or Diplomacy DC.\n\n---\nSuccess The mortal party receives one favor from the fiend, or the fiend becomes the mortal's minion for 1d4 days if they're on the same plane. Alternatively, if the GM allows the option, the mortal can receive a bargained contract of the fiend's level or lower.\n\nFailure The fiend caller fails to strike the bargain.\n\nCritical Failure The process fails, and the magical backlash makes the fiend caller Drained 2."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Fiendish Ritualist",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "A fiend caller can cast Binding Circle and Commune to contact fiends even though the rituals are beyond the normal rank the fiend caller could cast. Furthermore, they can use Legal Lore for the primary check when they do so instead of the listed skill."
    },
